{"version":"1","source":"Architectural Atlas procedural model","scope":"Sydney Harbour Bridge, Sydney (simplified schematic)","title":"Sydney Harbour Bridge","location":"Sydney, Australia","blurb":"The steel through arch bridge across Sydney Harbour, opened 19 March 1932, in simplified schematic form: the 503 m arch, hangers, 49 m deck, granite-faced pylons and skewback foundations.","sourceUrls":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Sydney Harbour Bridge","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sydney_Harbour_Bridge"},{"label":"Archive.org: The Story of the Sydney Harbour Bridge, 50th Anniversary","url":"https://archive.org/stream/the-story-of-the-sydney-harbour-bridge-50-th.-anniversary-1932-1982/The%20Story%20of%20the%20Sydney%20Harbour%20Bridge%2C%2050%20th.%20Anniversary%2C%201932%20-%201982_djvu.txt"}],"systems":[{"id":"arch","name":"Arch","color":"#7d8894","description":"The 503 m steel arch: two ribs in 28 panels, lateral bracing and hangers, rising 134 m above the harbour."},{"id":"deck","name":"Deck","color":"#5d6a75","description":"The 49 m wide deck with parapets across the 1149 m bridge."},{"id":"pylons","name":"Pylons","color":"#cfc7b4","description":"The four decorative 89 m pylons, concrete faced with granite."},{"id":"approaches","name":"Approach trestles","color":"#7d8894","description":"The steel trestles carrying the approach spans on each shore."},{"id":"foundations","name":"Foundations and bearings","color":"#9a958a","description":"The concrete skewbacks and the four main bearings."},{"id":"details","name":"Beacon","color":"#c23b2e","description":"The aircraft beacon at 141 m."}],"explanations":{"arch west rib":"The west arch rib: one of two 503 m steel ribs, each built in 28 panels of 18.28 m and rising 134 m above the harbour. Exact truss member sizes are schematic.","arch east rib":"The east arch rib: one of two 503 m steel ribs, each built in 28 panels of 18.28 m. Exact truss member sizes are schematic.","lateral bracing":"The cross-bracing tying the two arch ribs together against wind loads. Exact bracing pattern is schematic.","west hangers":"The west row of vertical hangers carrying the deck from the arch. The real hangers run from 7.3 m to 58.8 m; modeled lengths are schematic.","east hangers":"The east row of vertical hangers carrying the deck from the arch. Modeled lengths are schematic.","deck segment 1":"Western third of the main-span deck, 49 m wide. Exact lane arrangement is schematic.","deck segment 2":"Central third of the main-span deck. Exact lane arrangement is schematic.","deck segment 3":"Eastern third of the main-span deck. Exact lane arrangement is schematic.","rail tracks":"The two rail tracks carried on the deck. Exact track positions are schematic.","cycleway":"The cycleway on the deck. Exact position is schematic.","footway":"The pedestrian footway on the deck. Exact position is schematic.","south approach deck":"The south approach deck, part of the 1149 m total length. Exact span arrangement is schematic.","north approach deck":"The north approach deck, part of the 1149 m total length. Exact span arrangement is schematic.","west parapet":"The west parapet along the deck. Exact parapet form is schematic.","east parapet":"The east parapet along the deck. Exact parapet form is schematic.","south-west pylon shaft":"The shaft of the south-west pylon: the four decorative pylons stand 89 m above mean sea level, concrete faced with granite. Exact cross-section is schematic.","south-west pylon cap":"The cap of the south-west pylon. The pylons are decorative; the arch thrust goes into the skewbacks. Exact cap form is schematic.","south-east pylon shaft":"The shaft of the south-east pylon, concrete faced with granite. Exact cross-section is schematic.","south-east pylon cap":"The cap of the south-east pylon. Exact cap form is schematic.","north-west pylon shaft":"The shaft of the north-west pylon, concrete faced with granite. Exact cross-section is schematic.","north-west pylon cap":"The cap of the north-we